cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  This is a public-domain legislative research draft, released under CC0 1.0.
  Please cite the publication version and commit so readers can identify the
  text reviewed.
title: "Frontier Artificial Intelligence Officer Certification Act (Illinois research draft)"
abstract: >-
  A research draft amending Illinois's Artificial Intelligence Safety Measures
  Act, 430 ILCS 185 (P.A. 104-0538, as amended by P.A. 104-0466), to require
  named natural persons at large frontier developers to sign the compliance
  record Illinois already requires. The enacted Act requires an independent
  audit whose report must assess the developer's "designation and empowerment of
  senior personnel" at 430 ILCS 185/10(d)(2)(C) and must carry "the signature of
  the lead auditor" at 430 ILCS 185/10(d)(2)(G); no controlling officer of the
  developer signs anything, and the Act's principal civil penalties run only
  against the entity. The draft adds a deployment certification or truthful
  acknowledgment of noncompliance, a signed management response to each annual
  audit, personal and non-delegable duties of reasonable inquiry and response, a
  public officer-signature register, Attorney General enforcement against a
  required signer for breach of that signer's own duty, and personal payment of
  individual civil penalties without corporate indemnification, insurance,
  reimbursement, or compensation offset. It does not alter Illinois's
  10^26-operation compute threshold or $500,000,000 revenue threshold, does not
  regulate ordinary AI systems, does not impose liability merely because a
  company violated another provision, and creates no criminal offense and no
  private right of action. Public-domain research draft; never introduced or
  enacted; no completed review claimed.
